{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqqy7diwrc6","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"Root cause of the reported daemon \"wedge\" (GET /health times out, requests hang past their socket timeout) during subconscious assignment prepare, branch_task, attempt/feature merge, and the automode judge merge: lib/git.js ran every git command via execFileSync on the daemon's single event-loop thread. Measured on this repo (124 worktrees): `git worktree add` ~5.5s, `git worktree remove` ~2s, `git status` ~0.15s. For the whole duration of a worktree add the daemon serviced NO request, /health included — that is the wedge. It is NOT the search-context agentic path: 8 back-to-back search-context calls with no prepare kept the loop healthy (event-loop lag under 1.1s); an in-process probe showed 6.5-7.4s event-loop stalls 1:1 with each prepare's worktree add. Fix (branch worktree-fix-daemon-sync-git-wedge): added async execFile variants to lib/git.js (createWorktreeAsync, removeWorktreeAsync, mergeBranchAsync, createFeatureWorktreeAsync, mergeFeatureAsync, attemptDiffAsync, initRepoAsync, isRepoAsync, listWorktreesAsync) and made the already-async route handlers in routes/git.js, routes/task.js, routes/subconscious.js, routes/overlay.js await them; sync versions kept verbatim for CLI/tests. After the fix /health stays p50=4ms max=9ms while a 6s worktree add runs concurrently. Two secondary fixes in the same branch: search-context rebuilt the whole graph once PER agentic round because the daemon ctx exposed no readGraphSnapshot — added an overlay-mtime-cached readGraphSnapshot so the graph builds once per request (measured search latency climb 0.5s to 2.2s); and rerank/embed cold-start spawned duplicate sidecars (observed 3 rerank sidecars) because the _spawning flag clears before the child binds its socket — added a 15s spawn cooldown.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T18:41:06.141Z"}
